@startuml
title TH-01 Attack Tree - Account Takeover and Login Abuse

skinparam backgroundColor #f4f4f4
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam rectangle {
	BorderColor #5c5c5c
	FontColor #1f1f1f
	RoundCorner 8
}

rectangle "Attacker gains unauthorized\naccount access\n(TH-01)" as ROOT #e6f7ff

rectangle "Attacker executes brute-force\nagainst login endpoint\n(AC-01, AC-09)" as BRUTEFORCE #ffffff
rectangle "Attacker compromises and\nreplays authentication tokens\n(AC-02)" as TOKEN_REPLAY #ffffff
rectangle "Attacker abuses password\nreset lifecycle weaknesses\n(AC-10)" as RESET_ABUSE #ffffff

rectangle "Mitigate with rate limiting,\nlockout controls, and\nsecurity event logging\nControls: AC-006, LM-001\nTests: ST-010\nReq: RF-02, RNF-09" as M_BRUTEFORCE #d6f5ea
rectangle "Mitigate with token expiry,\nmandatory auth checks,\nHTTPS-only transport, and\nsecrets hardening\nControls: AC-002, AC-003, AC-005, SC-001\nTests: ST-002, ST-003, ST-005\nReq: RNF-02, RNF-03, RNF-05, RNF-23" as M_TOKEN_REPLAY #d6f5ea
rectangle "Mitigate with reset abuse\ndetection, rate limiting,\nand centralized logging\nControls: AC-006, LM-001\nTests: ST-010" as M_RESET_ABUSE #d6f5ea

ROOT -down-> BRUTEFORCE
ROOT -down-> TOKEN_REPLAY
ROOT -down-> RESET_ABUSE

BRUTEFORCE -down-> M_BRUTEFORCE
TOKEN_REPLAY -down-> M_TOKEN_REPLAY
RESET_ABUSE -down-> M_RESET_ABUSE

note bottom
Attack path logic:
- Branches from ROOT are OR alternatives.
- Each mitigation block defines the primary defensive response for that branch.
end note

@enduml
